  "narrative": {
    "summaryIntro": "Vaishno Devi Temple is located in a naturally formed cave on the Trikuta Mountains in the Udhampur district of Jammu and Kashmir. Dedicated to the goddess Durga (worshipped as Vaishno Devi, Mata Rani, or Trikuta), the temple is one of the most visited pilgrimage sites in India. The shrine houses three naturally formed rock formations believed to represent the three aspects of the goddess: Saraswati, Lakshmi, and Durga.\n\nThe pilgrimage to Vaishno Devi requires trekking approximately 12-14 kilometers through scenic mountain paths. The cave temple is situated at an altitude of 1,560 meters and attracts millions of pilgrims annually. The journey is considered spiritually rewarding, and the temple represents a perfect blend of natural geography and divine spirituality.",
